    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Air pollution makes life tougher for some insects and plants, a new study shows."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Researchers at the University of Washington conducted tests with the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "evening primrose",
            "zh": "月见草"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". At night, the pleasant smell of its flowers "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "interacts",
            "ref": "v-interact"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with certain air pollutants. Key scent "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "molecules",
            "zh": "气味分子"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " are destroyed "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This makes it hard for "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pollinators",
            "zh": "传粉者"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to find the flowers. The team shared its findings in "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Science"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, traffic, industry, and other human "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " release "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "pollutants",
            "ref": "v-pollutant"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " into the air. These include "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "ozone",
            "zh": "臭氧"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nitrogen oxides",
            "zh": "氧化氮"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". By day, sunlight breaks down much of the ozone. But in the dark, ozone "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "reacts",
            "ref": "v-react"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nitrogen dioxide",
            "zh": "二氧化氮"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the air. This produces short-lived, highly reactive "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nitrate radicals",
            "zh": "硝酸盐自由基"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In their experiment, the researchers put bags over evening primrose flowers to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their scent. They took the scent back to the lab, along with some "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "moths",
            "zh": "飞蛾"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that are naturally drawn to primrose flowers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In the lab, a wind tunnel was used to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "mimic",
            "ref": "v-mimic"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " conditions in an outdoor field. The researchers released the primrose scent and moths into the wind tunnel. At once, they watched the moths fly upwind, "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the scent."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But it was a different story when pollutants were "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The moths couldn’t fly in a straight line. They seemed to be looking for the scent—often without "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The team then studied the molecules of the primrose scent. They discovered two chemical signals that the moths use to find primrose flowers. When "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "exposed",
            "ref": "v-expose"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to nitrate radicals, both chemicals broke down. They then became much less "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to the moths. It’s like “blindfolding you and asking, ‘Can you go and get me a coffee?’” says Jose Fuentes, an "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "atmospheric scientist",
            "zh": "大气科学家"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " at Pennsylvania State University."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Other plants that depend on pollinators for "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "reproduction",
            "zh": "繁殖"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " are affected by this "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " as well. Among them are many food crops. This means pollution could pose a new type of threat to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", says Joel Thornton, an atmospheric scientist on the research team."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
